-- Formatter: `-` as negation and `-` as subtraction are different trees
-- (language.md §6.5) and the formatter must never print one as the other.
-- `f (-1)` is a call on a negated literal; `f - 1` subtracts from `f`;
-- `f (-1) (-2) -3` is a two-argument call minus three.
a f = f (-1)


b f = f - 1


c f x = f x - 1


d x y = x - -y


e2 x = -x - -1


g f = f (-1) (-2) - 3
